															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-cihan" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1383950); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1383950&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609016584" alt="Dr Cihan" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1383950)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-cihan" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1383950); return false;" >Dr Cihan</a></span> <span class="odate time_1342351851 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Jul 2012 11:30</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1508567">
									

<p>The only thing that disturbed me about this is that it is not &quot;containable&quot; or &quot;contained&quot; just plainly observed.<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Because this is written as a SCP I think that it has to be contained within the foundation.Since there is no possible way to contain it my opininon is it just belongs to an other class of anomaly.</span>The idea of using a confidental SCP to explain its observation made me a little jumpy but thats all.The main idea is a pretty commonly used one.In many fictions some sort of &quot;Mother Planet&quot; or an Organisms that creates planets can be seen</p>
<p>BUT</p>
<p>On the bright side even with a commonly used subject you made me read the article and that is a hard thing to do.Because it is so overused that people can just scroll down and say &quot;Meh just a giant yellow heart which poops out planets&quot;.The Addenda makes a good impression and stages are pretty clear to visualise.It is clinical and very well written.And that is very well enough for me.</p>
<p>I upvote because I liked the wording manner,clearness and this hard-to-accomplish-well-writing-with-an-overused-idea thing.<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">But I still think it should not be a SCP.</span></p>
<p>EDIT:Since there a lot of uncontained SCP's which cant be contained and the only difference with this is the distance.Meh a SCP is a SCP.Sorry to bother. Maybe there can be an other class like uncontained other than the SCP series because of nature of the word &quot;SCP&quot; Secure Contain Protect.But eh thats just my opinion :)</p>

							</div>

								
